  "assumptions": [
    "Kubernetes uses Cilium in native-routing mode with BGP to the NX-OS leaves (no VXLAN/Geneve tunnel), so pod IPs appear on the fabric and in NetFlow exported by the leaves. Cilium kube-proxy replacement translates Service ClusterIPs to backend pod IPs at connect time, so ClusterIPs do not appear on the wire.",
    "The NX-OS VXLAN fabric dc1-vxlan is managed by Nexus Dashboard; leaves export NetFlow to Splunk Stream.",
    "The ACI fabric aci-1 hosts the VM tier (orders database) in tenant shop, VRF prod, EPG db.",
    "Cisco FTD ftd-edge sits at the internet edge and performs DNAT for the public entry VIP and SNAT for outbound traffic.",
    "Isovalent Runtime Security (Tetragon) on the Cilium nodes emits processConnect events through the Cisco Security Cloud HEC input.",
    "Cilium routing mode is undecided for the pilot. Conversations marked encapsulation=vxlan model tunnel mode: the fabric sees only node-to-node UDP 8472, and inner pod tuples are available only from Isovalent."
  ],
